AndroidiOS <p>A liquid pill that bridges between bottom-nav items as the selection changes.</p> <pre><code>val state = rememberGooeyNavIndicatorState(selectedIndex = 0)

GooeyNavIndicatorHost(state = state, color = Mint) {
    NavigationBar {
        tabs.forEachIndexed { index, tab -&gt;
            NavigationBarItem(
                modifier = Modifier.gooeyNavItem(state, index),
                selected = state.selectedIndex == index,
                onClick = { state.select(index) },
                icon = { /* ... */ },
            )
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>

AndroidiOS <p>The same liquid pill, bridging between segmented control options as the selection changes.</p> <pre><code>val state = rememberGooeySegmentedControlState(selectedIndex = 0)

GooeySegmentedControlHost(state = state, color = Mint) {
    Row {
        options.forEachIndexed { index, label -&gt;
            Box(
                Modifier
                    .gooeySegmentItem(state, index)
                    .clickable { state.select(index) },
            ) { Text(label) }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>

AndroidiOS <p>Wrap the screen in a <code>GooeyTransferHost</code>, mark each source row with <code>GooeySource</code>, and give the target card a <code>GooeyTarget</code>. Tapping (or long-press-dragging) a source transfers its token.</p> <pre><code>val state = rememberGooeyTransferState()

GooeyTransferHost(state = state) {
    Column {
        GooeyTarget(state = state, cornerRadius = 28.dp) {
            TransferredTokens()
        }

        LazyColumn {
            items(friends, key = { it.id }) { friend -&gt;
                GooeySource(
                    state = state,
                    key = friend.id,
                    color = friend.tint,
                    cornerRadius = 16.dp,
                    token = { Avatar(friend) },
                ) {
                    FriendRow(friend, avatarModifier = Modifier.tokenAnchor())
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>tokenAnchor()</code> marks where inside the row the flying copy visually starts from.</p>
